WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Fold the top of your ear
forward, then let go.

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.000
It springs straight back into shape.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.410
Every time you land from a jump,
pads inside your knee take the load.

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.460
And discs between the bones of
your spine let your back flex.

5
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.620
All three are made of cartilage.

6
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.740
So how can one tissue spring
back, cushion and flex?

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.920
In this mission, you'll
look inside cartilage:

8
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.580
living cells, each in
its own space, in a firm,

9
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.610
rubbery matrix with no
blood vessels at all.

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.450
Then you'll map the five
jobs of your skeleton,

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.600
from protecting your brain
to making red blood cells.

12
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.250
Your mission: find out how
one tissue can spring back,

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.870
cushion and flex.
